title: 'How to Hire Remote Developers in India: Employment, Contractors and EOR Explained'
publishedAt: 2026-11-11
type: companies
---
**Quick answer:** A foreign company can hire remote developers in India in three main ways: as **independent contractors** (fast and simple, but risky if the person works like a full-time employee), through an **Employer of Record (EOR)** that legally employs them for you (compliant and quick, for a monthly fee), or by setting up your **own Indian entity** (most control, but costly and slow). Most startups start with an EOR or carefully structured contracts. To hire well, post salaries in rupees, plan around notice periods of 30 to 90 days, set clear overlap hours, and screen for async communication as well as technical skill.

India has one of the largest pools of software engineers in the world, with strong talent across backend, frontend, mobile, data, DevOps and AI. Many global startups now hire their first engineers there. The opportunity is real, but so are the legal, payment and cultural details.

*This article is general information, not legal or tax advice. Employment rules change, so check with a qualified advisor for your situation.*

## Why companies hire developers in India

- **A large, experienced talent pool**, from fresh graduates to engineers who've built products at global scale.
- **English as a working language** in most tech teams.
- **Time zone overlap** with Europe in the afternoon and the Middle East during the day, and partial overlap with the US with planning.
- **A strong startup ecosystem**, so many engineers have startup experience.
- **Competitive costs**, though senior engineers in India are well paid and the gap with other markets is narrowing.

